## Finding and bounded BUILD path

The accepted five-minute current-source capture still fails AC-4's maximum-gap condition: 6,050 matched frames over 302.506666 seconds, 20.000523 fps mean cadence, 89.163715 ms maximum EOF gap, and 753 of 6,049 gaps above 60 ms. The latest sequential traced 600-frame A/B found a modest difference with output-side `-flush_packets 1`: read gaps above 60 ms fell from 122/599 to 107/599 and the maximum fell from 88.425 ms to 86.679 ms; write-boundary counts fell from 120/599 to 106/599 with the maximum down from 88.367 ms to 86.696 ms. Both arms still have many >60 ms gaps. Since the arms were sequential and straced, this does not prove a causal or repeatable effect and does not authorize a production argv change.

The revision-3 package proposes a read-only 600-frame ABBA repeat on `/dev/video60`: default (A), `-flush_packets 1` (B), B, A. Keep all other FFmpeg arguments, queue/thread settings, mode, and reader fixed; apply identical tracing; save no payload; make no source edit. The result is diagnostic only and cannot pass AC-4. Preserve `timestampEof` as host-monotonic time after complete raw-frame read; FFmpeg PTS remain V4L2 SOE, not EOF.

## Open evidence limits

- The initial output-flush A/B was sequential, traced, and unpaired; observer overhead and order/run variation may explain some or all of the small delta.
- The proposed ABBA diagnostic has not been run and will not isolate FFmpeg internal decode/filter/synchronization waits or identify the output writer thread.
- DQBUF trace counted 602 successful dequeues for 600 outputs and omitted sequence fields, so exact dequeue-to-output identity is unproven.
- AC-4 remains failed on the accepted five-minute reproduction. AC-6 reconnect/sibling continuity and AC-8 four-camera soak/CPU headroom remain hardware deferrals. The existing minor FFmpeg child resource-limit finding remains open.

## Next consumer

Submit this revision-3 package to `gatekeeper-admiral` for `investigation-review`. If approved, route the bounded read-only ABBA diagnostic to `build/build-management`; no production source/argv change is requested by this package.

